# Template for this stack's shared/secrets.env on prodbox. Copy to
# /opt/apps/pitchbox-landing/prod/shared/secrets.env, fill in the real ORIGIN,
# `chmod 600` it. release.sh reads this file and copies it (plus the release-pinned
# LANDING_IMAGE/APP_VERSION/APP_COMMIT) into every releases/<sha>/.env, but never
# writes to this file itself. This file is never committed; only this template is.
#
# There is no secret in this file. It holds two plain config values, not a
# credential: LANDING_PORT (the loopback port the container publishes on) and
# ORIGIN (the public URL SvelteKit needs behind Caddy's reverse proxy). No
# database and no mail sender either, because the way in is an account on
# app.pitchbox.app (decided on #423). It stays a file rather than a hardcoded
# default so whatever lands after this issue and needs its own config (a real
# second stack on the reserved 5284, an analytics key, anything else scoped to
# this repo) has one place to add it without touching release.sh -- and so a
# real secret, when one eventually lands here, has the same place to live
# rather than a new mechanism invented for it.
#
# Port convention: 5184 is this repo's prod stack, verified free on prodbox on
# 2026-09-09; pitchbox itself owns 5180-5183 (that repo's scripts/deploy.sh) and
# canonry-landing owns 5195/5295. 5284 is reserved for a second stack under this
# repo, not yet built - see docker/Caddyfile.example.

LANDING_PORT=5184

ORIGIN=https://pitchbox.app
